			"Message": "docs(Mist): Restructure README with Compatibility section, code formatting, and badge additions\n\nAdd a new Compatibility table documenting Mist's integration with Mountain, Air, Cocoon, and SideCar. Add Crates.io and Rust Version badges beneath the License badge for quick package visibility.\n\nApply consistent backtick formatting for proper nouns throughout the document (`editor.land`, `Node.js`, `JSON`, `gRPC`, `DnsPort`), bringing the README inline with sibling component conventions. Fix the mermaid diagram by removing doubled line-escape backslashes. Update the SideCar entry in the Integration table with its 🌏 emoji for visual consistency with adjacent rows.\n\nReorganise the Dependencies table by removing the Version column (versions drift vs. Cargo.toml) and retitling it to Key Dependencies. Restructure the blockquote quote attribution to sit directly under the emphasised line rather than in a nested paragraph. Correct the Project Structure tree by stripping the `Element/` prefix (Mist already is an Element) and adding a root `Cargo.toml` entry. Update the Vine reference emoji from 🍇 to 🌿 and bold the API Reference link. Add a CHANGELOG link to the Related Documentation section and remove the Project Maintainers footer.\n\nSource presentation and discoverability improvements only — no functional changes.",
